<title>SOUTH KOREA: New S.Korean port to boost grain trade with China.</title>
<headline>New S.Korean port to boost grain trade with China.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Plans to establish a new port on the west coast of the Korean peninsula will boost South Korea's grain trade with China, the U.S. embassy said on Friday.</p>
<p>The U.S. agricultural attache said in a report the new port would include construction of grain silos with a total capacity of 150,000 tonnes by 1998 and 200,000 tonnes by 2000.</p>
<p>&quot;These facilities -- located directly across from the coast of China -- would provide for expanded opportunities for China-Korea grain trade in the future,&quot; the report said.  </p>
<p>South Korea has been the leading buyer of Chinese corn this year, with purchases reaching an estimated 1.2 million tonnes so far and projected to rise to 2.0 million tonnes by end-September.</p>
</text>
